# Spock specs

Write feature tests as Spock `*Spec.groovy` in `src/test/groovy` (same package as production). English only.

## Feature method name

`def` must be `Given ..., When ..., Then ...` (capital G/W/T, comma-separated). Do not use a plain sentence.

```groovy
// BAD
def "returns summaries from the catalog port"() { ... }

// GOOD
def "Given the catalog port returns a Zelda summary, When the service searches for zelda, Then the summaries are returned unchanged"() { ... }
```

## Blocks

Use `given:`, `when:`, `then:` with an English description on each. Prefer `when`/`then` over `expect`.

```groovy
given: "the catalog port will return a Zelda summary"
def summaries = [new GameSummary(123L, "Zelda", 2017, "https://cover")]

when: "the service searches for zelda"
def results = service.search("zelda")

then: "the summaries from the catalog are returned unchanged"
1 * gameCatalogPort.search("zelda") >> summaries
results == summaries
```

`contextLoads` stays JUnit. Do not invent extra test layers beyond the spec.
